      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Letting it go\" means accepting that the effort required to keep it running is no longer worth the outcome. If the system is constantly crashing, the noise and the errors are just symptoms of a fundamental, unfixable flaw. Sometimes the only true resolution is to cease the attempt, to pull the plug and find a different, more stable environment.",
      "source": "target",
